WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.637
After checking the basic structure, we can build a quick profile of the data.

00:00:04.637 --> 00:00:13.602
The describe function summarizes a numeric column with information such as count, mean, standard deviation, minimum,

00:00:13.602 --> 00:00:22.092
maximum, and quartiles. For categorical columns, value counts tells us how often each value appears.

00:00:22.092 --> 00:00:27.072
The number of unique values tells us how many distinct categories exist.

00:00:27.072 --> 00:00:33.747
These simple checks are part of exploratory data analysis because they help us understand distributions and identify

00:00:33.747 --> 00:00:36.707
suspicious values early.

00:00:36.707 --> 00:00:42.692
For example, if a sales channel should have only web, email, and store, but the unique count is six,

00:00:42.692 --> 00:00:46.865
we should investigate before continuing.
